gpu_edram_bookkeeping_memo (off by default, hot reload): every draw marks the EDRAM tiles of each render target it
writes dirty and adds stencil bits to them (a loop over ~700 tiles each). Both are idempotent, and consecutive draws to
the same render targets repeat them: a range within one of the last four ranges set dirty since tiles were last made
clean, or within the render target's last stencil addition with no new bits since its bits were last set, is skipped.
Counters in the gpu_frame_stats log.

